---
# yamllint disable rule:line-length
# Lifts the user's own `boxed()` into a `Φ.hone.box`, stamped `minted ↦ "user"`.
#
# FOUR rules mint a box and they are not interchangeable, which is what the
# binding records (#1016): `206` a `boxed()` the user wrote, `208-mapToObj` the
# crossing from a primitive stream to a reference one, `211` the head of the
# sandwich it splits a lambda-carrying primitive operator into, and `214` the
# head of the one it puts around a `distinct()` or a `skip(n)`. Every box now
# says which, and the rules that read a box say which ones they want:
#
#   * `209` folds an unbox and a box into a boxing distill — a genuine user
#     round trip, so `"user"` and `"crossing"` only. Handed a `"split"` or a
#     `"sandwich"` it splices a stray `Wrapper.valueOf` into the middle of a
#     primitive chain, which its own header has warned about since it was
#     written; ordering alone did not prevent it, because the whole rule set
#     runs to a fixpoint and `209` gets another turn after `211` and `214` fire.
#   * `221-unbox-box-to-map` cancels an unbox against the box behind it —
#     anything but `"user"`.
#   * `221-unbox-user-box-to-map` takes `"user"`, and only with an unbox pinned
#     behind it.
#   * `411`, the two `443-unsandwich` rules and `602` want a box whoever minted
#     it, and bind the value without reading it.
#
# #1016 is what the missing distinction cost: a primitive `distinct()` or
# `skip(n)` with a `boxed()` right behind it ends `214`'s sandwich in an unbox,
# `221` cancelled that unbox against the user's box and kept only the unbox, and
# the boxing the user asked for was gone — `501` then lowered the run to
# `mapMultiToInt` while the caller held the `Stream` `boxed()` had promised, and
# the first element threw `IncompatibleClassChangeError`.
name: boxed-to-box
pattern: |
  ⟦
    φ ↦ Φ.jeo.opcode.invokeinterface,
    𝜏-target-stream-class ↦ 𝑒-target-stream-class,
    𝜏-method ↦ "boxed",
    𝜏-result-stream-class ↦ "()Ljava/util/stream/Stream;",
    𝜏-flag ↦ Φ.true
  ⟧
result: |
  ⟦
    φ ↦ Φ.hone.box,
    stream-class ↦ 𝑒-target-stream-class,
    minted ↦ "user"
  ⟧
when:
  or:
    - eq: [𝑒-target-stream-class, '"java/util/stream/IntStream"']
    - eq: [𝑒-target-stream-class, '"java/util/stream/LongStream"']
    - eq: [𝑒-target-stream-class, '"java/util/stream/DoubleStream"']
